WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- Hey, guys, it's YB.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.420
I'm in Korea.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.610
It's my first time being back in 10 years.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.280
I was born in Seoul, South Korea,

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.290
and then I moved to America when I was 12,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.210
and I came back briefly when I was 14,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.910
but since then, I haven't been back.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.430
The thing is, I'm not in Seoul.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.690
I'm in Jeju, which is
like the island of Korea.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:16.640
My parents moved here,

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.830
and it's actually my
first time being in Jeju.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.400
I'll do what I do best, eating.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.858
So, I'll show you guys
what I eat on this island

00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:23.715
and all the experiences I have.

00:00:23.715 --> 00:00:25.132
So, come with me.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.110
So, for breakfast, we
went to Paris Baguette.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.780
In Korean, it's Paris Baguette

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.770
It's a bakery super popular in Korea.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.100
I think there are some in America too,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.510
but they're Korean bakeries.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.480
They had some of the breads
I used to grow up on.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.623
This is one of them.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.790
See, it's shaped like Hawaiian bread,

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.473
but inside there's kind
of cheese layers in it.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.933
There is this pastry with sweet
potatoes in it, really good.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.150
This is my favorite,
it's called soboro-ppang.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.630
It's known for the bumpy crust,

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.280
and it tastes like peanut butter.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.320
This is tteokbokki, spicy rice
cake along with fish cake,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.120
dumplings, and boiled eggs.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.923
This one also has ramen in it.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.400
Korean fried chicken.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.210
This one is sweet and spicy,
called gangjeong chicken.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.830
This one is a regular fried
chicken called huraideu

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.050
and my favorite, soy sauce chicken.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.810
It's called ganjang chicken.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.733
They're crunchy and juicy
with perfect amount of salty,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.983
and we ate two whole chickens.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.310
So, Cheju-do is a volcanic island,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.560
meaning it was formed
by volcanic eruptions.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.396
That's why there are a
lot of rocks everywhere.

00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:32.229
(speaking Korean)

00:01:46.511 --> 00:01:49.560
So, I got a guide to learn
more about the rocks.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.490
It says Jusangjeolli is
a column-shaped joint

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.913
that commonly develops in
basaltic rocks in a lava flow.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.850
These tall statues are all over Jeju

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.373
and are called dol hareubang,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.593
which translates into stone grandpa.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:03.970
They're made from hyunmuam,

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.460
the volcanic rocks with holes
my mom just talked about,

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.330
and they're know to protect the island.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.570
And also, I found out about this

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.690
after I posted a picture
hugging one of them,

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.420
people commented about the statues

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.580
very closely resembling a penis,

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.070
and apparently there's a
myth that dol hareubangs

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.130
were indeed shaped after a
penis, and if you rub their nose,

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.580
you will give birth to a son.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.203
Thanks, guys, for the info.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.930
So, we're gonna try black pork today.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.490
In Jeju, it's really famous.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.430
How you tell is there's hair on the meat,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.430
that's how you tell it's the black pork.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.453
Looks like regular pork belly.

00:02:40.342 --> 00:02:41.175
Wow.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.923
So chewy, super tender, so good.

00:02:50.911 --> 00:02:51.744
- Mm!

00:02:52.146 --> 00:02:54.219
(laughing)

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.873
- This is seafood heaven.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.683
Sushi buffet, all you can eat.

00:02:59.386 --> 00:03:01.470
Here we are at Hamdeok Beach.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.113
Look how clear the water is!

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.470
It's still a little cold to go swimming,

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.720
but didn't stop me from
getting in the water.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.280
Here is nakji-bokkeum
which is spicy octopus,

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.362
nakji-pajeon, which is
Korean pancakes with octopus,

00:03:15.362 --> 00:03:16.463
and dumpings.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.863
You fry it perfectly and very crispy.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.370
You can taste the protein.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.080
This is kalguksu, a
traditional Korean noodle dish.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.780
It literally means knife noodles.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.070
Kal is knife and guksu is noodle.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.050
It's made with knife-cut wheat noodles.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.360
Usually, the color's white,

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.763
but this one has mulberry
leaf, so it's green.

00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:38.497
(speaking Korean)

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.387
So, now we're at (speaking Korean),

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.920
which is Seogwipo's National
Recreational Forest.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.180
But this is just actually
a small part of Hallasan,

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.660
which is a mountain in Jeju,

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.613
and Hallasan is the highest
mountain in South Korea.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.500
So, for dinner, we'e going
to (speaking Korean),

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.320
which is apparently really
famous for mackerel sashimi,

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.710
which is very uncommon.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.867
It's located at a fishing port in Jeju

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.907
called (speaking Korean).

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.066
As you can see, there
are tons of boats here.

00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:07.773
This is the famous mackerel sashimi,

00:04:07.773 --> 00:04:11.033
(speaking Korean) in Korean,
and all the side dishes here.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.450
They're right from the ocean,
so they taste clean and fresh.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.543
The plain seaweed and spiced
scallion make perfect combo.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.730
After the sashimi, they
give you a mackerel soup.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.603
It's peppery, spicy, and super savory.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.750
So, my mom and I are
gonna go get some lunch.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.540
We're gonna go look at Porch.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.147
It's chuk in Korea.

00:04:35.147 --> 00:04:38.633
- It's called the Sick Pickle
because it helps digestion.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.620
- Yeah, so it's good when you're sick,

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.570
but good also when you're not sick.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.947
- These are potato skin dumplings.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.783
And my mom got octopus kimchi porridge.

00:04:57.109 --> 00:04:58.109
- Mm, yummy.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.440
- And mine is called maesaengi soup.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.543
Maesangi is a type of
seaweed that's in Korea,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.920
that's what makes it green.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.000
Hot, but very good.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.400
Oh my God, look at all
these Korean snacks.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.313
This is heaven.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.707
This is one of my favorite
snacks, or even a quick meal,

00:05:18.707 --> 00:05:19.540
Samgak-gimbap.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.010
It translates into triangle bimpap

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.610
like a sushi roll, but triangle.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.840
They sell it at any convenience stores,

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.290
and there are many flavors,
but this one is tuna.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.193
It's so good.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.350
Welcome to a Korean family feast.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.620
These are just the appetizer side dishes.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.054
The main course is this one,

00:05:37.054 --> 00:05:40.003
Maeuntang, which is a spicy fish soup.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.063
The broth is the best with rice.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.420
The giant tower of rocks
over there is Oedolgae,

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.593
which basically means a lonely rock.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.063
It's 20 meters or 66 feet tall.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.100
It does look a little lonely by itself,

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.500
but I think it's beautiful.

00:05:55.847 --> 00:05:57.420
So, today's my last day here.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.860
I'm about to go back to L.A.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.350
and I'm really sad that
it's come to an end,

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.293
but I had so much fun
exploring Jeju Island.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.577
I learned so many new
things on this island,

00:06:05.577 --> 00:06:07.808
and it was great to get back
in touch with my culture,

00:06:07.808 --> 00:06:10.360
and most importantly, the food was great.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:11.730
So, thanks, guys, for coming with me.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:12.670
I hope you enjoyed it,

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:15.080
and hopefully I can travel
to another country soon.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.053
So, until next time, Korea.

00:06:17.315 --> 00:06:19.898
(upbeat music)

